plugin-hostd-full (0.20.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pull requests since 0.20.7: #9 (the RPM and DEB builds run by
    workflow_dispatch only, make check on pull requests in lint.yml), #12
    (floors only: every dependency a floor, no ceiling, the same in the spec
    and debian/control; tests/ranges.py refuses a ceiling or a pin), #15 (the
    commit-msg hook is the shared stub byte for byte), #17 (release.yml reads
    the same-pass list through the shared same-pass action, with
    tests/release_same_pass.py holding it), #19 (Fedora 45 only, the F44 cells
    dropped, and a lint refusing any F44 cell), #20 (the commit identity check
    is on for pull requests).
  * Floors moved: plugin-hostd >= 0.20.8 (was 0.20.7), omx-clap-host >= 0.33.0
    (was 0.32.3); this package uses no omx-clap-core, so that floor is not
    set here.
  * New dependency: plugin-hostd-protocol >= 0.7.0 (published 0.7.0; the
    pre-cut named 0.6.0).
  * Conflicts, Breaks, Replaces and Obsoletes: none, and none naming our
    packages.
  * Unchanged floors: omx-plugins >= 0.19.3, plugin-qualify >= 0.20.1,
    recommended omx-panel >= 0.13.0 and plugin-qualification-records >=
    2026110902.

